  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The team has room counts, visitor comments, and volunteer observations from the weekend.\", \"decision\": \"How should the museum choose a small improvement?\", \"goal\": \"Help visitors find a satisfying route through the museum while keeping reception and volunteers manageable.\", \"problem\": \"A volunteer-run local museum wants to make a weekend visit easier to navigate. It has a modest collection, printed guides, a reception table, flexible volunteer positions, and several rooms that can remain open independently. The decisions concern interpretation and visitor organization, not conservation rules or safety policy.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe team starts with the busiest room and uses comments and observations to choose an improvement. The change addresses a place with demonstrated pressure.\nThe team proposes an improvement and asks which counts, comments, and observations would support trying it. The proposal is tested against the available evidence.\nThe team starts with repeated comments and checks room counts and observations before choosing an improvement. The change addresses an experience supported by broader records."
    }
  ],
